    content: `<h2>What USDT is</h2><p>USDT is a cryptoasset issued by Tether that aims to stay close to one US dollar. This peg is its target: the buy or sell price can differ from US$1. Buying, holding and selling USDT can result in losses.</p><p>It can be used to transfer tokens or trade on platforms that support it. The amount received depends on the available price and transaction costs.</p><h2>Backing and redemption</h2><p>Tether states that its tokens are backed by reserves including cash, equivalents and other assets. The June 30, 2026 reserves report has BDO assurance over selected information at that date. Separately, on August 13, 2026, Tether announced a full KPMG U.S. audit of Tether International, S.A. de C.V.’s 2025 financial statements. These documents have different scopes.</p><p>Direct redemption requires verified-customer status and compliance with Tether’s terms. As of October 15, 2026, the published minimum is US$100,000 and the fee is the greater of US$1,000 or 0.1%. Selling through P2P is a separate transaction with its own prices and terms.</p><h2>🌐 Networks and compatibility</h2><p>USDT exists on several networks. Before transferring, verify the token and its contract in Tether’s official <a href="https://tether.to/en/supported-protocols/" rel="noopener">protocol list</a>, and confirm that both services support the same network.</p><p>The list covers different Tether assets: a network appearing there does not prove it supports native USDT. Wrapped or third-party tokens add other dependencies. Check the current transaction’s fee and requirements rather than using a fixed figure from this guide.</p><h2>🇧🇴 What to check from Bolivia</h2><p>When comparing a BOB transaction with a USDT transaction, identify which asset you would receive and how you could use or convert it afterward. A USDT payment requires the recipient to accept it.</p><p>Availability, limits and verification depend on the service and your account. Check its terms and applicable rules. Compare timing and total cost with the other options available to you.</p><h2>Risks to understand</h2><p>USDT carries issuer, platform and custody risks. Redemption or transfers may face restrictions or delays. The tokens are not insured bank deposits. A price close to the dollar does not guarantee recovery of the amount invested.</p><h2>📊 How to compare stablecoins</h2><p>To compare products, review the issuer, how it describes its reserves, its published documents, who can redeem and under what conditions. Also examine networks, custody, restrictions and the costs of the service you would use.</p><p>A “stable” label does not replace those checks. This guide does not rank any stablecoin as universally safer or more liquid.</p><h2>🎯 Possible uses and their conditions</h2><ul><li><strong>Transfers:</strong> Both parties must support the token and network. Check the time and cost of sending and converting it.</li><li><strong>Payments:</strong> Confirm acceptance, amount, network and refund terms with the recipient.</li><li><strong>Trading:</strong> Some platforms offer USDT pairs; switching to USDT does not guarantee preservation of gains.</li><li><strong>Holding:</strong> The value you could recover depends on the price, costs and access to your funds.</li></ul><h2>🔒 Custody options</h2><ul><li><strong>Third-party custody:</strong> A provider manages access. Review its terms, withdrawals and response to failure or insolvency.</li><li><strong>Self-custody:</strong> You manage the keys. Losing or exposing them can cause permanent loss.</li><li><strong>Online or offline wallets:</strong> These carry different risks. A physical device can be lost, damaged or stolen; it does not guarantee absolute security.</li></ul><p>Choose only after understanding the risks and access recovery. The balance alone does not determine a suitable option.</p><h2>⚠️ Common Mistakes to Avoid</h2><ul><li>Confusing USDT with cash or a dollar deposit.</li><li>Sending without checking the asset, address, network and any required memo.</li><li>Assuming an incorrect transfer can be reversed.</li><li>Sharing private keys or a recovery phrase.</li><li>Ignoring fees, restrictions and who controls the keys.</li></ul><h2>💰 Products offering yield</h2><p>Holding USDT and using a product that offers yield are separate decisions. Before considering one, identify who receives the assets, how it earns income, what losses you could face and when withdrawals are allowed.</p><p>Risks include provider failure, technical failures and loss of principal. Rates can change; an advertised annual figure does not guarantee the result. This guide does not recommend a provider or publish expected returns.</p><h2>📈 Keep information current</h2><p>Check reserve-report dates and scope, redemption terms, supported networks and service conditions before trading. A general guide cannot confirm that a feature or withdrawal is available for a particular account.</p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Before using USDT, distinguish the token, its market price and direct redemption with the issuer. Check each service’s costs, withdrawal terms and custody risks. This guide is educational and does not recommend allocating any portion of your savings to USDT.</p><div style="background: #ECFDF5; padding: 16px; border-radius: 8px; margin-top: 24px;"><p><strong>💡 Next step:</strong> Read our <a href="/blog/guide-buy-dollars-binance-p2p?lang=en">guide to buying USDT with bolivianos on Binance P2P</a>.</p></div><h2>Sources</h2><p>Checked October 15, 2026. Availability and terms can change.</p><ul><li><a href="https://tether.to/en/legal/" rel="noopener">Tether token terms</a></li><li><a href="https://tether.to/en/fees/" rel="noopener">Tether fees</a></li><li><a href="https://tether.to/en/legal/?tab=risk-disclosure-statement" rel="noopener">Tether current risk disclosure</a></li><li><a href="https://assets.ctfassets.net/vyse88cgwfbl/2kYf7r64h3tzwiu6F0CbUB/2997abd2f11ecea74a21528048b50707/Opinion___Report_-_Tether_International_Financial_Figure_30-06-2026.pdf" rel="noopener">BDO June 2026 reserve assurance report</a></li><li><a href="https://tether.io/news/tether-completes-the-largest-inaugural-financial-audit-in-history/" rel="noopener">Tether announcement of 2025 full financial audit</a></li><li><a href="https://tether.to/en/supported-protocols/" rel="noopener">Tether Supported Protocols and Integration Guidelines</a></li><li><a href="https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/general-resources/news-alerts/alerts-bulletins/investor-bulletins/investor-bulletin-crypto-asset-interest-bearing-accounts" rel="noopener">Investor.gov Crypto Asset Interest bearing Accounts</a></li><li><a href="https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/general-resources/news-alerts/alerts-bulletins/investor-bulletins/crypto-asset-custody-basics-retail-investors-investor-bulletin-0" rel="noopener">SEC Crypto Asset Custody Basics for Retail Investors</a></li><li><a href="https://www.binance.com/en/support/faq/detail/115003670492" rel="noopener">Binance crypto withdrawal instructions</a></li></ul>`,
